window.VD=window.VD||{};window.VD["audi/q7-4l"]={"q7-4l-facelift-120-km-h-overtaking-alert":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_q7_4l_facelift-0de3e545.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>To activate or deactivate a message reminding you that you are exceeding the 120km/h speed limit.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.  </p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:  </strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“17 – Instruments</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Wizard</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select byte<strong>“0”</strong> <br/>Then check to enable or uncheck to disable the box in<strong>“6”</strong>:<strong>“Speed warning at 120 kph (75 mph) active</strong>”.  </p>","q7-4l-facelift-acc-distance-control-in-mmi":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_q7_4l_facelift-0de3e545.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to change the distance of the Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) on the menu in Audi MMI 3G.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>Select</strong> ” and run the VCDS program. <strong><strong>13 – Distance control</strong></strong> ” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Choose <em><strong>Channel 7</strong> </em>then set the value to <strong>1</strong></p>\n<p><em>Restart MMI (MENU + CAR 10 sec).</em></p>\n<p><em>For the cruise control menu, press CAR then driver assistance then Adaptive cruise control, you can choose “Distance” 4 distance selection modes</em>.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_7452-7b2530cd.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_7166-a399eb74.webp\"/></figure>","q7-4l-facelift-activate-bluetooth-audio-streaming-a2dp-mmi-3gp":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_q7_4l_facelift-0de3e545.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Enables Bluetooth streaming audio on the MMI 3G PLUS, so you can listen to music from your A2DP-compatible audio player.  </p>\n<p><em>ATTENTION: You must have activated the Hidden Menu (<a href=\"https://www.vag-coding.fr/audi/q7-4l/q7-4l-facelift-activer-menu-cache-mmi-3gp/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Activate hidden menu MMI 3GP</a>)</em> and enabled Bluetooth (either by default or via the “Activate Bluetooth MMI 3GP” tutorial).  </p>\n<p>Press CAR + MENU (for 6s)  </p>\n<p>diagnose -&gt; settings -&gt; ami_aux -&gt; Select <strong>AMI BT [enabled] 1/2</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_mmi_3gp_bluetooth_ami_bt-8fa46d9c.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>bluetooth -&gt; Check <strong>A2DP Activation</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_mmi_3gp_bluetooth_ad2p-90e760bc.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>Restart MMI</p>\n<p><em>Press MENU + Wheel + Top Right button.</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_mmi_3gp_bluetooth_ad2p_v2-660aabbb.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_mmi_3gp_bluetooth_ad2p_v3-6ac58876.webp\"/></figure>","q7-4l-facelift-activate-dvd-playback-while-driving-vim":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_q7_4l_facelift-0de3e545.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Allows you to remove the MMI protection and continue watching a DVD or video while driving (Video in Motion).   </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Step 1: Recovering the MMI 3GP serial number</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “Select”.<strong>5F-Computer-electr. </strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Advanced Ident -1A</strong>”.</p>\n<p>Retrieve serial number (if more than one, use the <strong>first</strong> one!)</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a1_8x_mmi_plus_5f_seriennummer-PNG-12291981.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Step 2: Calculating the security code</strong></p>\n<p>Enter the serial number previously retrieved from the website (your choice, subject to availability):  </p>\n<p>–&gt; <a href=\"https://www.audienthusiasts.com/Articles_VIM.html\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">AUDIENTHUSIATS VIM</a></p>\n<p>–&gt; <a href=\"https://www.bestcarmods.com/vim/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">BESTCARMODS VIM</a></p>\n<p>The site will display your security code.<br/><em>An alternative security code is also generated.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Step 3: Enter security code</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “Select”.<strong>5F-Computer-electr. </strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Secure access -16</strong>”.</p>\n<p>Enter security code <br/><em>(Use alternative security code if first code does not work)</em></p>\n<p><strong>Step 4: Removing the protection</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “Select”.<strong>5F-Computer-electr. </strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation -10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5 – </strong>Select Channel <strong>48</strong> </p>\n<p><em>Set value to <strong>255</strong></em></p>\n<p><strong>Step 5: Restart the MMI</strong></p>\n<p>Simultaneously press MENU + Wheel + Top right button</p>","q7-4l-facelift-activate-mmi-3gp-cd-dvd-extraction":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Audi Q7 4L facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_q7_4l_facelift-0de3e545.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Activates CD/DVD extraction in the DVD player. Allows you to import / copy all CD/DVD / SD card content to the MMI 3G PLUS jukebox (hard disk).   </p>\n<p><strong>To continue, you must first activate the hidden MMI menu (Green Menu).</strong></p>\n<p><em><em>To activate the MMI hidden menu (Green Menu) :</em> <a href=\"#/audi/q7-4l/q7-4l-facelift-activate-mmi-3gp-hidden-menu\">Activate MMI 3GP hidden menu</a></em></p>\n<p>Press <strong>CAR + SETUP</strong> for 6 sec to bring up the hidden menu.</p>\n<p>diagnose -&gt; settings -&gt; import_multimedia -&gt; Tick <strong>Ripping</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_mmi3g_plus_hidden_menu_cd-ripping-cbf13d3b.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Restart MMI</strong></p>\n<p><em>Press MENU + Wheel + Top Right button.</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/import_ripping_mmi3g_vagcoding-af2ca0fd.webp\"/></figure>","q7-4l-facelift-activate-mmi-3gp-hidden-menu":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_q7_4l_facelift-0de3e545.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Enables the hidden green menu (green menu, hidden menu, test mode, engineer mode) in the Audi MMI 3G PLUS. </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>Select</strong> “, then click on ” <strong>Select</strong> “. <strong>Procedure:</strong> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<strong><strong>5F – Information Electr.</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em><strong>Channel 6</strong> </em>and set the value to <strong>1</strong></p>\n<p><em>No need to restart the MMI.</em></p>\n<p><em><em>To open the Hidden Menu, press MENU + CAR (simultaneously for 6 seconds), or press the CAR button first.</em></em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/a7_mmi_plus-bb5ba729.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_navigation_plus_mmi3g_hidden_menue-ae4ebd5e.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Note:</strong> <strong>Never</strong> select the “Bootloader” option!</p>\n<p><strong><a href=\"#/t/access-the-audi-red-engineering-menu\">–&gt; To access the Audi Red Engineering menu</a></strong></p>\n<p><a href=\"#/t/enabling-the-hidden-menu-for-audi-mmi-3g-and-3g\"><strong>–&gt; Enable the hidden MMI 3G/3G+ menu without VCDS or OBDeleven</strong></a></p>","q7-4l-facelift-activate-stationary-heater":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_q7_4l_facelift-0de3e545.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: activates stationary heating and its management on the MMI.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>Select</strong> ” and run the VCDS program.<strong><strong>08 – Auto HVAC</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>” then <strong>“Long Coding Helper”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select Byte<strong> 2 </strong>:</p>\n<p>Bit<strong> 3 </strong>: Check box<em> </em></p>","q7-4l-facelift-activating-ambient-lighting":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Audi Q7 4L facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_q7_4l_facelift-0de3e545.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: activates ambient lighting and its management via MMI.  </p>\n<p><strong>The hidden menu must be activated</strong> (See: <a href=\"https://www.vag-coding.fr/audi/q7-4l/q7-4l-facelift-activer-menu-cache-mmi-3gp/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Activate hidden menu MMI 3GP</a> )</p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong> <strong>Activate mood lighting</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “Select”. <strong><strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong> “Long Coding Helper”</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em>Byte <strong>16</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>6</strong>: Tick “Interior/Ambiance Lighting Adaptation active”.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 2: Activate the MMI menu</strong></p>\n<p>Launch the Hidden Menu by pressing MENU + CAR (for 6s)</p>\n<p>car -&gt; carmenuoperation -&gt; interior light -&gt; select “5”.</p>\n<p>Press “Return</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/interior_light_hidden_menu_mmi3g-8680e758.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>  car -&gt; cardevicelist -&gt; interior light -&gt; check box</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/interior_light_hidden_menu_mmi3g1-9f0f03ff.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>  car -&gt; carbusassignment -&gt; Interior light -&gt; Select [CAN Komfort] 1/9</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a5_8t_facelift_hidden_menu_car_carbusassignme-331aee89.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>Reboot the MMI by pressing MENU + Wheel + Top Right Button.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_mmi_reset-f3d493fd.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 3: Ambient lighting control from MMI</strong></p>\n<p><strong>How it works:</strong></p>\n<p><em>Ambient lighting</em><br/><em> – is permanently activated when the light control switch is in OFF position.</em><br/><em> – switches on/off automatically when the headlamp switch is in AUTO position.</em><br/><em> – will never light up to 100% (even when maximum lighting is selected).</em><br/><em> – lights up to 100% when doors are opened.</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a5_8t_facelift_setup_fussraumbeleuchtung-1639c23f.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a5_8t_facelift_dimmung_fussraumbeleuchtung-2d9373cb.webp\"/></figure>","q7-4l-facelift-activation-of-gearshift-recommendation":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_q7_4l_facelift-0de3e545.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Activates the gearshift recommendation. The gearshift recommendation is then displayed in the lower section of the ODB.   <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“17 – Instruments</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>” .<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select byte<strong>“1</strong>“<br/>Then check Bit<strong>“5</strong>“.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/check_aiguille-9b803756.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_7102-675f485c.webp\"/></figure>","q7-4l-facelift-bluetooth-mmi-3gp-activation":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_q7_4l_facelift-0de3e545.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to activate Bluetooth with an Audi MMI 3G PLUS.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>To continue, you must first activate the hidden MMI menu (Green Menu).</strong></p>\n<p><em>To activate the MMI hidden menu (Green Menu) : <a href=\"https://www.vag-coding.fr/audi/q7-4l/q7-4l-facelift-activer-menu-cache-mmi-3gp/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Activate MMI 3GP Hidden Menu</a></em></p>\n<p><strong>Step 1: Activate Bluetooth in the hidden menu</strong></p>\n<p>Press <strong>CAR + MENU</strong> for 6 sec to bring up the hidden menu.</p>\n<p>diagnostics  &gt;  settings  &gt;  tel_settings -&gt;  Select  “<strong>HFP activation</strong><br/>diagnosis  &gt;  settings  &gt;  tel_settings -&gt;  Select  “<strong>BT activation</strong><br/>diagnosis  &gt;  settings  &gt;  tel_settings -&gt;  Select  <strong>“BT defaut visibility” to [auto] 1/3</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_mmi_3gp_tel_settings-af0d9718.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>diagnose -&gt; settings -&gt; ami_aux -&gt; Select <strong>AMI BT [enabled] 1/2</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_mmi_3gp_bluetooth_ami_bt-8fa46d9c.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Step 2: Restart MMI</strong></p>\n<p><em>Press MENU + Wheel + Top Right button.</em></p>\n<p><br/><strong>Step 3: Bluetooth activation with VCDS</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong> and then click on ” “.<strong><strong>5F – Information Electr.</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Choose <em><strong>Channel 17</strong> </em>then set the value to <strong>1</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Module_5F_Adaptation_Channel17-d3fc3a63.webp\"/></figure>","q7-4l-facelift-change-mmi-3gp-start-logo":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_q7_4l_facelift-0de3e545.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to change the Splash Screen of the MMI 3G PLUS.  </p>\n<p><em>For a custom logo see tuto: Q7 (4L) – MMI 3G/3GP custom start logo</em></p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> </p>\n<p><strong>To continue, you must first activate the hidden MMI menu (Green Menu).</strong> </p>\n<p><em>To activate the MMI hidden menu (Green Menu) : <a href=\"https://www.vag-coding.fr/audi/q7-4l/q7-4l-facelift-activer-menu-cache-mmi-3gp/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Activate MMI 3GP Hidden Menu</a></em></p>\n<p><strong>Step 1: Change the start logo in the hidden menu</strong></p>\n<p>Press <strong>CAR + SETUP</strong> for 6 sec to bring up the hidden menu.</p>\n<p>car -&gt; carcodingvehicle -&gt; Select No Of Screen</p>\n<p><em>Select the desired display:</em><br/><em><br/>0 -&gt;  Standard display<br/>1 -&gt;  Standard display<br/>2 -&gt;  A8<br/>3 -&gt;  S8<br/>4 -&gt;  W12<br/>5 -&gt;  A6<br/>6 -&gt;  S6<br/>7 -&gt;  RS6<br/>8 -&gt;  A6 allroad<br/>9 -&gt;  A7<br/>10 -&gt;  S7<br/>11 -&gt;  RS7<br/>12 -&gt;  A1<br/>13 -&gt;  S1<br/>14 -&gt;  Q3<br/>15 -&gt;  A4<br/>16 -&gt;  A4 allroad<br/>17 -&gt;  S4<br/>18 -&gt;  RS4<br/>19 -&gt;  A5<br/>20 -&gt;  S5<br/>21 -&gt;  RS5<br/>22 -&gt;  Q5<br/>23 -&gt;  Q5 Hybrid<br/>24 -&gt;  Q7<br/>25 -&gt;  Q7 Hybrid<br/>26 -&gt;  SQ5<br/>27 -&gt;  Standard display<br/>28 -&gt;  Standard display<br/>29 -&gt;  Standard display</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/splashscreenmmi3gp-6fcb5f6a.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><br/><strong>Step 2: Restart MMI</strong></p>\n<p>Simultaneously press SETUP or MENU (1) + Central knob (2) + Top right knob (3)</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/redemarrermmi3g-18d07873.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_Vierge-e6bcc4e4.webp\"/></figure>","q7-4l-facelift-headlamp-washer-settings":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_q7_4l_facelift-0de3e545.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to set the delay time before the headlamp washer emerges / the duration of the headlamp washer spray / the number of activations.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1 (Headlamp washer activation time) :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20113</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click “ <strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Select <em><strong>Channel 25</strong>: </em> </p>\n<p><em>Set value to </em><strong><em>“</em>8000”</strong> or value of your choice (default: 2000 ms)  </p>\n<p><strong>Line 2 (Headlamp washer spray duration) :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20113</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click “ <strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Select <em><strong>Channel 06</strong>: </em> </p>\n<p><em>adjust value accordingly (in ms)</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 3 <strong>(Number of activations before headlamp washer) :</strong></strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20113</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click “ <strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Select <em><strong>Channel 26</strong>: </em><br/><em>adjust the value for the number of times the headlamp washer must be switched on manually before activation.</em></p>","q7-4l-facelift-lowering-the-passenger-mirror-when-reversing":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_q7_4l_facelift-0de3e545.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> automatically lowers the passenger mirror when reversing.  </p>\n<p>The mirror adjustment knob must be in position<strong>“R”</strong> for the passenger mirror to lower automatically.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“52 – Passenger door</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select byte<strong>“4</strong>”<br/>Then check Bit<strong>“2</strong>”:<strong>“Reserve Gear Mirror Dipping active</strong>”<br/>and Bit<strong>“3</strong>”:<strong>“Position Memory for Reserve Gear Mirror Dipping active</strong>”.<br/></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Golf-7-Abaisser-le-retroviseur-passager-lors-de-la-9710a97c.webp\"/></figure>","q7-4l-facelift-microphone-sensitivity-adjustment":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Audi Q7 4L facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_q7_4l_facelift-0de3e545.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to adjust the intensity of the hands-free system’s microphone.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong><strong>For MMI 2G :</strong></strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“77 – Telephone</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – On this page, at the top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose Channel <strong>131</strong> or <strong>07</strong>.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom of the page.<br/>On this menu, choose a value expressed in<strong>“dB</strong>” (default value<strong>“0 dB</strong>”) then validate.</p>\n<p><strong>For MMI 3G :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>To continue, you must first activate the hidden MMI menu (Green Menu).</strong></p>\n<p><em>To activate the MMI hidden menu (Green Menu) : <a href=\"#/audi/q7-4l/q7-4l-activate-mmi-3g-hidden-menu\">Activate MMI 3G Hidden Menu</a></em></p>\n<p>Press <strong>CAR + SETUP</strong> for 6 sec to bring up the hidden menu.</p>\n<p>main &gt; diagnostics &gt; settings &gt; Mic sensiblity  </p>\n<p>Choose a value between : -6db/0db/+6db</p>\n<p><strong>Restart MMI</strong></p>\n<p>Simultaneously press SETUP (1) + Central knob (2) + Top right knob (3)</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/redemarrermmi3g-18d07873.webp\"/></figure>","q7-4l-facelift-needle-check":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_q7_4l_facelift-0de3e545.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to activate the scanning of the speedometer needles when the car is started. (Needle Sweep)  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“17 – instruments</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select byte<strong>“1</strong>”<br/>Then check Bit<strong>“0</strong>”:<strong>“Gauge Test/Needle Sweep active</strong>”.<br/></p>\n<figure>\n</figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/check_aiguille-9b803756.webp\"/></figure>","q7-4l-facelift-oil-temperature-via-lap-timer":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_q7_4l_facelift-0de3e545.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to add oil temperature to the stopwatch menu on the ODB screen.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“17 – Instruments</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>” .<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select byte<strong>“1</strong>”<br/>Then check Bit<strong>“3</strong>”:<strong>“Lap Timer active</strong>”.</p>\n<figure>\n</figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/check_aiguille-9b803756.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_q7_4l_facelift_lap_timer-be199aba.webp\"/></figure>","q7-4l-facelift-opening-closing-windows-with-remote-control":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_q7_4l_facelift-0de3e545.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Enables you to open and close the windows and sunroof using the remote control. </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong></strong> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click<strong>“46 – Comfort Module.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Encoding – 07</strong>,” then click “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select byte “<strong>2</strong>“<br/>Then check bit “<strong>2</strong>“</p>","q7-4l-facelift-remove-belt-alarm":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_q7_4l_facelift-0de3e545.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: To suppress the audible alarm and the warning light on the speedometer when driving without a seatbelt.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select</strong>”, then click on “<strong>17 – Instruments</strong>”. 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>” then “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select Byte <strong>0</strong>:</p>\n<p>Bit <strong>2-4</strong>: select <strong>“Seat Belt Warning inactive”</strong> from the drop-down list.</p>\n<figure>\n</figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/voyant_ceinture_de_securite-296648a9.webp\"/></figure>","q7-4l-facelift-speed-of-radar-deactivation-or-reversing-camera":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_q7_4l_facelift-0de3e545.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: Selects the speed at which radar and/or reversing camera are deactivated.  </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>10 – Assistance stationn</strong>”.  <br/><br/><strong>4 – </strong>Click on <strong>“Adaptation – 10”</strong> </p>\n<p>5 – Select<strong> Channel 23 or 233 from </strong>the list of values</p>\n<p><strong>6 –</strong> Choose a value between <strong>0 and 20 km/h</strong></p>","q7-4l-activate-battery-charge-status-in-the-mmi":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Activates battery charge status in Audi MMI Basic / 2G / 3G / 3GP.  <br/></p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/></p>\n<h2>MMI Basic (Radio Symphony/Concert) :</h2>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “Select”.<strong><strong>56 – Radio</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Choose <em><strong>Channel 39</strong> </em>then increase the value by <strong>+16</strong></p>\n<hr/>\n<h2>MMI 2G :</h2>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “Select”.<strong><strong>07 – Control Head</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Choose <em><strong>Channel 01</strong> </em>then adjust the value accordingly:</p>\n<p>x1xxxxxx = show battery status display<br/>x0xxxxxx = do not show battery status display</p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Select <em><strong>Channel 02</strong> (Installation List II (MMI Functionnality) </em>then increase the value by <strong>+32</strong></p>\n<p><em>Restart the MMI (Press SETUP + Wheel + Top Right Button)</em></p>\n<p><em>If the battery does not appear after restarting the MMI, launch the hidden menu (to activate it, see the “activate hidden menu” tutorial, to launch the hidden menu press MENU + CAR (for 6s)).</em></p>\n<p>DIAG SETTINGS -&gt; Car Menus Maske -&gt; Battery Level-&gt; Check box</p>\n<hr/>\n<h2>MMI 3G / 3GP :</h2>\n<p><em><strong>WARNING: </strong>You must have activated the Hidden Menu<a href=\"https://www.vag-coding.fr/audi/q7-4l/q7-4l-activer-menu-cache-mmi-3g/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">(Activate MMI 3G hidden menu</a>).</em></p>\n<p><em>To launch the Hidden Menu press MENU + CAR (for 6s)</em></p>\n<p>car -&gt; carextdevicelist -&gt; battery -&gt; check box</p>\n<p>car -&gt; carmenuoperation -&gt; battery -&gt; select <strong>5</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Audi_MMI3g_PLUS_Hidden_Menue_battery-5a0d0626.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>Restart MMI</p>\n<p><em>Press SETUP + Wheel + Top Right Button.</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/mmi3g_reset-cdd6298b.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/batterieMMI2g-b0e8bfbc.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Audi_MMI_3G_PLUS_batterie-69d82b4b.webp\"/></figure>","q7-4l-activate-daytime-running-lights-drl-on-mmi":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to activate/deactivate the daytime running lights (DRL) on the MMI.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>Select</strong> ” and run the VCDS program.<strong><strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p>4 – Click on “Coding – 07” then “Long Coding Helper”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – <em><em>Put <strong>2 in </strong>the penultimate digit of the code (0xxxx<strong>?</strong>x).</em></em></p>\n<p>-&gt; 2 = with Daytime Running Lights (selectable via MMI)</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/a6c6centralelec-1024x630-dac2c92a.webp\"/></figure>","q7-4l-activate-dvd-playback-while-driving-vim":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Allows you to remove the MMI protection and continue watching a DVD or video while driving (Video in Motion).   </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Step 1: Recovering the MMI 3G serial number</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “Select”.<strong>5F-Computer-electr. </strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Advanced Ident -1A</strong>”.</p>\n<p>Retrieve serial number (if more than one, use the <strong>first</strong> one!)</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a1_8x_mmi_plus_5f_seriennummer-PNG-12291981.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Step 2: Calculating the security code</strong></p>\n<p>Enter the serial number previously retrieved from the website (your choice, subject to availability):  </p>\n<p>–&gt; <a href=\"https://www.audienthusiasts.com/Articles_VIM.html\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">AUDIENTHUSIATS VIM</a></p>\n<p>–&gt; <a href=\"https://www.bestcarmods.com/vim/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">BESTCARMODS VIM</a></p>\n<p>The site will display your security code.<br/><em>An alternative security code is also generated.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Step 3: Enter security code</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “Select”.<strong>5F-Computer-electr. </strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Secure access -16</strong>”.</p>\n<p>Enter security code <br/><em>(Use alternative security code if first code does not work)</em></p>\n<p><strong>Step 4: Removing the protection</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “Select”.<strong>5F-Computer-electr. </strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation -10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5 – </strong>Select Channel <strong>48</strong> </p>\n<p><em>Set value to <strong>255</strong></em></p>\n<p><strong>Step 5: Restart the MMI</strong></p>\n<p>Simultaneously press MENU + Wheel + Top right button</p>","q7-4l-activate-mmi-2g-hidden-menu":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Enables the hidden menu (green menu, hidden menu, test mode, engineer mode) in the Audi MMI 2G. </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition switched off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostic port.<br/><br/><strong></strong> 2 – Turn on the ignition, then launch the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click<strong>“07 – Display/Control.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em><strong>Channel 08 </strong></em>and set the value to <strong>1</strong></p>\n<p><em>Reboot the MMI by pressing SETUP + the Dial + the Upper-Right Button</em></p>\n<p><em>To open the Hidden Menu, press MENU + CAR (for 6 seconds)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/menu_cache_mmi2g-42dff347.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong><a href=\"#/t/access-the-audi-red-engineering-menu\">–&gt; To access the Audi Red Engineering menu</a></strong></p>","q7-4l-activate-mmi-3g-cd-dvd-extraction":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Activates CD/DVD extraction in the DVD player. Allows you to import / copy all CD/DVD / SD card content to the MMI 3G jukebox (hard disk).   </p>\n<p><strong>To continue, you must first activate the hidden MMI menu (Green Menu).</strong></p>\n<p><em>To activate the MMI hidden menu (Green Menu) : <a href=\"#/audi/q7-4l/q7-4l-activate-mmi-3g-hidden-menu\">Activate MMI 3G Hidden Menu</a></em></p>\n<p>Press <strong>CAR + SETUP</strong> for 6 sec to bring up the hidden menu.</p>\n<p>diagnose -&gt; settings -&gt; import multimedia -&gt; selectionner <strong>[Copy/Ripping] 4/4</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Audi_MMI3g_PLUS_diagnose_settings_importmultimedia-01b4e47b.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><br/><strong>Restart MMI</strong></p>\n<p>Simultaneously press SETUP or MENU (1) + Central knob (2) + Top right knob (3)</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/redemarrermmi3g-18d07873.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/import_ripping_mmi3g_vagcoding-af2ca0fd.webp\"/></figure>","q7-4l-activate-mmi-3g-hidden-menu":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Enables the hidden green menu (green menu, hidden menu, test mode, engineer mode) in the Audi MMI 3G. </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition switched off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostic port.<br/><br/><strong></strong> 2 – Turn on the ignition, then launch the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click<strong>“5F – Electrical Information.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em><strong>Channel 6</strong> </em>and set the value to <strong>1</strong></p>\n<p><em>No need to restart the MMI.</em></p>\n<p><em><em><em><em><em>To open the Hidden Menu, press MENU + CAR (simultaneously for 6 seconds), or press the CAR button first.</em></em></em></em></em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/a7_mmi_plus-bb5ba729.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/mmi3g-217db9e1.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Note:</strong> <strong>Never</strong> select the “Bootloader” option!</p>\n<p><strong><a href=\"#/t/access-the-audi-red-engineering-menu\">–&gt; To access the Audi Red Engineering menu</a></strong></p>","q7-4l-activate-mood-lighting":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: activates ambient lighting and its management via MMI.  </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong> <strong>Activate mood lighting</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “Select”.<strong><strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong> “Long Coding Helper”</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em>Byte <strong>16</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>6</strong>: Tick “Interior/Ambiance Lighting Adaptation active”.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 2: Activate the MMI menu</strong></p>\n<p><em><strong>For Radio Symphony/Concert</strong></em></p>\n<p>[56 – Radio] -&gt; [Coding- 07] -&gt; [Long Coding Helper].</p>\n<p><em>Byte 8 : </em><br/><em>Bit 7: “Interior Light Settings active” checkbox</em></p>\n<hr/>\n<p><em><strong>For MMI Basic Plus</strong></em></p>\n<p>[07 – Control Head] -&gt; [Coding – 07]  </p>\n<p><em>Add “<strong>2</strong>” to the penultimate digit of the coding (old coding: <strong>0164201</strong>, new coding: <strong>0164221</strong>).  </em></p>\n<hr/>\n<p><em><strong>For MMI 2G</strong></em></p>\n<p>[07 – Control Head] -&gt; [Adaptation – 10] -&gt; Channel 01</p>\n<p><em>Add “2” to the existing value</em></p>\n<hr/>\n<p><em><strong>For MMI 3G</strong></em></p>\n<p><strong>The hidden menu must be activated</strong> (see: <a href=\"https://www.vag-coding.fr/audi/q7-4l/q7-4l-activer-menu-cache-mmi-3g/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Activating the MMI 3G hidden menu</a> ).</p>\n<p>car -&gt; carmenuoperation -&gt; interior light -&gt; select “5”.</p>\n<p>Press “Return</p>\n<p>  car -&gt; cardevicelist -&gt; interior light -&gt; check box</p>\n<p>Reboot the MMI by pressing SETUP + Wheel + Top Right Button.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 3: Ambient lighting control from MMI</strong></p>\n<p><strong><em>For MMI 3G</em></strong></p>\n<p><strong>How it works:</strong></p>\n<p><em>Ambient lighting</em><br/><em> – is permanently activated when the light control switch is in OFF position.</em><br/><em> – switches on/off automatically when the headlamp switch is in AUTO position.</em><br/><em> – will never light up to 100% (even when maximum lighting is selected).</em><br/><em> – lights up to 100% when doors are opened.</em></p>","q7-4l-automatic-headlight-activation-from-140-km-h":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>to automatically switch on the lights when the vehicle is travelling at over 140 km/h. </p>\n<p>(The lights will automatically go out if the vehicle is travelling at less than 60 km/h) </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “2 EPIRBs” module from the drop-down list and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>0</strong> Bit <strong>0</strong>: Check “Highway Light Function active above (140kph/90mph)”.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a5_8t_stg09_auswahl-steuergerate-rls-wws-bord-c6f10e6e.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a5_8t_stg09_bordnetz_rls_autobahnlicht_regenl-c0c525c9.webp\"/></figure>","q7-4l-automatic-headlight-activation-in-the-event-of-rain":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>to automatically turn on the lights when it’s raining and the wipers have been triggered.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “2 EPIRBs” module from the drop-down list and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>0</strong>, Bit <strong>1</strong>: Check “Rain Light Function Active”.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a5_8t_stg09_auswahl-steuergerate-rls-wws-bord-c6f10e6e.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a5_8t_stg09_bordnetz_rls_autobahnlicht_regenl-c0c525c9.webp\"/></figure>","q7-4l-aux-in-activation-retrofit":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to activate the AUX (Auxiliary) socket on the rear of the MMI 2G 3G 3GPLUS, for retrofitting to CarPlay / Android Auto / MP3 / BT box / AUX cable. You’ll also see “AUX” as an option in the multimedia menu on the central screen once you’ve completed the activation process.   </p>\n<p>When installing a CarPlay and Android Auto box kit on your MMI, you may wish to enable the AUX pin on the head unit on some cars (normally cars equipped with the Audi AMI multimedia interface). <br/>Note: if you have the Audi AMI interface, you can also use an AMI-AUX adapter instead of activating AUX. This will work fine, but you’ll need to run a cable to the AMI input. Although this works correctly, the cable is not hidden.    <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<h2><strong>For MMI 2G / 3G</strong></h2>\n<p><strong>To continue, you must first activate the hidden MMI menu (Green Menu).</strong></p>\n<p><em>To activate the hidden MMI menu (Green Menu) the tutorial is available according to your MMI model</em> <em>in the vehicle list.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Step 1: Activate AUX in the hidden menu</strong></p>\n<p>Press <strong>CAR + MENU</strong> for 6 sec to bring up the hidden menu.</p>\n<p><strong><em>MMI 2G : </em></strong>DIAG SETTINGS -&gt; APK 0x01, -&gt; Stereo Aux In <em>(Check)</em> -&gt; accept changes <em>(to validate the modification)</em></p>\n<p><strong><em>MMI 3G :</em></strong> diagnose -&gt; settings -&gt; ami_aux -&gt; Select <strong>AUX [enabled] 1/2</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_mmi_3gp_ami_bt-fdaa8044.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Step 2: Restart MMI</strong></p>\n<p><em>Press MENU + Wheel + Top Right button.</em></p>\n<hr/>\n<h2>For MMI 3G / 3GP</h2>\n<p><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – Select byte<strong>“8</strong>“<br/>Check bit<strong>“4</strong>” AUX-IN [PR-UE3] <em>to activate your MMI AUX output</em></p>\n<p><em>Uncheck AMI bit<strong>“5”</strong>[PR-UE7] if you’re using a Carplay box without an AMI adapter and you have the original AMI plug.</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Activater-AUX-616c1060.webp\"/></figure>","q7-4l-bluetooth-mmi-3g-activation":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to activate Bluetooth with an Audi MMI 3G.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>To continue, you must first activate the hidden MMI menu (Green Menu).</strong></p>\n<p><em>To activate the MMI hidden menu (Green Menu) : <a href=\"https://www.vag-coding.fr/audi/q7-4l/q7-4l-activer-menu-cache-mmi-3g/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Activate MMI 3G Hidden Menu</a></em></p>\n<p><strong>Step 1: Activate Bluetooth in the hidden menu</strong></p>\n<p>Press <strong>CAR + SETUP</strong> for 6 sec to bring up the hidden menu.</p>\n<p>main &gt; diagnostics &gt; settings &gt; Tel settings misc</p>\n<p>Select [no WLAN / no NAD / BT / HFP] 4 /16</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2: Restart MMI</strong></p>\n<p>Simultaneously press SETUP (1) + Central knob (2) + Top right knob (3)</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/redemarrermmi3g-18d07873.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><br/><strong>Step 3: Bluetooth activation with VCDS</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong> and then click on ” “.<strong><strong>5F – Information Electr.</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Choose <em><strong>Channel 17</strong> </em>then set the value to <strong>1</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Module_5F_Adaptation_Channel17-d3fc3a63.webp\"/></figure>","q7-4l-change-mmi-3g-start-logo":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to change the Splash Screen of the MMI 3G.  </p>\n<p><em>For a custom logo see tuto: Q7 (4L) – MMI 3G/3GP custom start logo</em></p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> </p>\n<p><strong>To continue, you must first activate the hidden MMI menu (Green Menu).</strong> </p>\n<p><em>To activate the MMI hidden menu (Green Menu) : <a href=\"https://www.vag-coding.fr/audi/q7-4l/q7-4l-activer-menu-cache-mmi-3g/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Activate MMI 3G Hidden Menu</a></em></p>\n<p><strong>Step 1: Change the start logo in the hidden menu</strong></p>\n<p>Press <strong>CAR + SETUP</strong> for 6 sec to bring up the hidden menu.</p>\n<p>car -&gt; carcodingvehicle -&gt; configuration line</p>\n<p><em>Select the desired display:</em></p>\n<p><em>[<strong>unknown] 1/5</strong> (Standard home screen)</em><br/><em>[<strong>standard] 2/5</strong> (Standard welcome screen)</em><br/><em>[<strong>S-line] 3/5</strong> (Standard welcome screen)</em><br/><em>[<strong>S-model] 4/5</strong> (S welcome screen depending on model)</em><br/><em>[<strong>RS-Model] 5/5</strong> (RS welcome screen)</em></p>\n<p>Then <em>select “Update Splashscreen (according car line)”.</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_6875-a1c0ed3d.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_6876-ad94c126.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_6877-7c285f46.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_6878-168e78a3.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><br/><strong>Step 2: Restart MMI</strong></p>\n<p>Simultaneously press SETUP or MENU (1) + Central knob (2) + Top right knob (3)</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/redemarrermmi3g-18d07873.webp\"/></figure>","q7-4l-change-start-logo-mmi-2g":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to change the Splash Screen of the MMI 2G.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>The hidden menu must be activated</strong> (see: <a href=\"#/audi/q7-4l/q7-4l-activate-mmi-2g-hidden-menu\">Activating the MMI 2G hidden menu</a> ).</p>\n<p>Launch the Hidden Menu by pressing SETUP + CAR (for 6s)</p>\n<p><br/>DIAG SETTINGS -&gt; HU Codierung -&gt; Standby-Bild -&gt; choose value</p>\n<p><em>Coding :</em></p>\n<p>0: Standard MMI 2G screen<br/>1: S6<br/>2: S5<br/>3: RS6<br/>4: RS logo</p>\n<p>Restart the MMI by pressing SETUP + Wheel + Top Right Button.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/mmi3g_reset-cdd6298b.webp\"/></figure>","q7-4l-correction-of-odb-consumption-display":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to correct the fuel consumption display on the on-board computer.  </p>\n<p><strong>Modification only possible on Mid/High range models</strong>. <br/><em>Note: modifications affect the display of instantaneous consumption, average consumption and fuel quantity.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select</strong>”, then click on <strong>“17 – Instruments”</strong>. <strong>Procedure:</strong> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation- 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 03</strong> <em>“Consumption Correction”.</em></p>\n<p><em>Adjust consumption correction factor between 85% and 115%.</em> <em>(base value: 100)</em></p>\n<p><em>Example 1: Calculation based on volume per distance (e.g. l/100 km): DIS: 9.3 l/100 km. Actual: 9.8 l/100 km. (100, 9,8 / 9,73 ? 105,38) Channel 3 will be changed from 100 to 105 <br/>Example 2: Calculation based on volume distance (e.g. MPG is: DIS: 23 MPG. Actual: 24 MPG. (100, 23/24 and 95.83) Channel 3 will be changed from 100 to 96</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/correction-consommation-odb-d51db18e.webp\"/></figure>","q7-4l-deactivate-rear-wiper-when-reversing":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to deactivate automatic activation of the rear windshield wiper during reversing when the front windshield wipers are operating.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/>3 – Click on ” <strong>Select</strong> “, then click on ” <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>” . Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program. 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em><strong>Channel 16</strong>: </em> </p>\n<p><em>Set value to </em><strong><em>“0</em>”</strong> to deactivate and <strong>“1”</strong> to activate  </p>","q7-4l-delete-belt-alarm":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: To suppress the audible alarm and the warning light on the speedometer when driving without a seatbelt.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select</strong>”, then click on “<strong>17 – Instruments</strong>”. 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Put <strong>0</strong> in the penultimate digit of the coding (xxxxx<strong>?</strong>x).</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/voyant_ceinture_de_securite-296648a9.webp\"/></figure>","q7-4l-disable-nav-phone-warning-messages-when-entering-while-driving":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to suppress navigation and telephone warning messages on the MMI when entering data while driving.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>Select</strong> “, then click on ” <strong>Select</strong> “. <strong>Procedure:</strong> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<strong><strong>5F – Information Electr.</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em><strong>Channel 2 and 3</strong> </em>then set the value to <strong>250</strong>.</p>","q7-4l-flash-mode-lights-during-emergency-braking":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: activates the brake/turn signal lights in flash mode during emergency braking.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“46- Central Conv.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong> “Adaptation – 10”</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 50</strong> (Adaptive Brake Light in the drop-down list)</p>\n<p><em>Add up the following values: </em><br/>+1 : Activate brake light flashing<br/>+2 = Brake light surface amplification<br/>+3 = Emergency brake flashing and brake light surface amplification</p>","q7-4l-lock-cd-dvd-eject-button-on-mmi-2g":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: locks/unlocks the CD/DVD eject button on the MMI 2G.  </p>\n<p><em>Protection against theft of your navigation DVD.  </em></p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>Select</strong> ” and run the VCDS program. <strong><strong>37 – Navigation</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em><strong>Channel 68</strong> (Ejection Lock)</em> then set the value to <strong>1</strong> <em>(Eject Button inactive (Anti-Theft))</em></p>\n<p><em>Restart the MMI 2G.</em></p>\n<p>To eject the CD/DVD, set the value to <strong>0</strong> for normal use of the button.  </p>","q7-4l-locking-unlocking-confirmation-beeps":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Used to set confirmation of door locking/unlocking with beep (alarm).  </p>\n<p><strong>The vehicle must be equipped with the factory-installed alarm</strong>.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong></strong> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click<strong>“46 – Comfort Module.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “ <strong>Code 07.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – <em>Add <strong>2048</strong> to the existing value</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/4L0-910-289_Module46_Coding-c9601d6e.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong> then click on “<strong>46 – Module Confort</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong> Adaptation – 10</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select Canal <strong>63</strong></p>\n<p><em>Add <strong>04</strong> to the value </em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/4H0-907-064_Module46_Adaptation_Channel63-5a820df9.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_mmi_3g_bip_verrouillage-090b7974.webp\"/></figure>","q7-4l-mmi-2g-speed-alert-and-odb-display":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Activates the display of the speed alert setting and on-board computer activation on the MMI 2G screen.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>The hidden menu must be activated</strong> (see: <a href=\"#/audi/q7-4l/q7-4l-activate-mmi-2g-hidden-menu\">Activating the MMI 2G hidden menu</a> ).</p>\n<p>Launch the Hidden Menu by pressing SETUP + CAR (for 6s)</p>\n<p>DIAG SETTINGS -&gt; APK 0x01, 0x0B, 0x0C -&gt; Bordcomputer -&gt; Check box</p>\n<p>Scroll to the bottom of the menu<br/>Select “Accept changes”.</p>\n<p><strong>Restart MMI</strong></p>\n<p>Press SETUP + Wheel + Top Right Button.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/mmi3g_reset-cdd6298b.webp\"/></figure>","q7-4l-mmi-3g-3gp-customized-start-logo":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: To modify and/or customize the home screen logo (Custom Splash Screen) with a personalized image of the MMI 3G and 3GPLUS. <br/><br/>Start by downloading the script file: <a href=\"https://www.vag-coding.fr/download/MMI_3G_3GP_SplashScreen_VAG-Coding.fr.zip\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">MMI_3G_3GP_SplashScreen_VAG-Coding.en.zip</a></p>\n<p><strong>Proceed </strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Then extract the file you just downloaded: MMI 3G 3GP SplashScreen VAG-Coding.en.zip</li>\n<li>Go to the “splashscreens” folder and edit the “startup_generic.png” image if you wish. You can edit this image, modify it or import another image, to have your own startup logo (keep the same PNG format and image size 800×480) or an image found in the “samples” folder (copy it into the “splashscreens” folder with the name startup_generic.png. </li>\n<li>Copy the contents of the MMI_3G_3GP_SplashScreen folder to a FAT32-formatted SD card (max. 32GB).</li>\n<li>Start your AUDI and let the MMI boot up, it takes a few seconds.</li>\n<li>Disconnect your smartphone’s Bluetooth if there’s a link between it and the MMI, and remove all your SD cards (SD1 &amp; SD2)…</li>\n<li>Then insert the SD card you have prepared into slot SD1.</li>\n<li>You’ll see green text asking you to turn the large knob on your MMI central console, and the message will disappear.</li>\n<li>Wait a few moments. A new message will appear stating that all has gone well and that your image has been imported successfully. </li>\n<li>Restart the MMI using the button combination that corresponds to your AUDI.<br/>Example: Press SETUP or MENU (1) + Central knob (2) + Top right button (3) at the same time.</li>\n</ul>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/redemarrermmi3g-18d07873.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>If your new start-up screen does not appear when your MMI reboots, go to the green hidden menu<em> (to activate the hidden menu, follow the “Activate MMI 3G or 3GP hidden menu” tutorial).</em></p>\n<p>For <strong>MMI 3GP </strong>: Select in <strong>car </strong>-&gt;<strong> carcodingvehicle </strong>-&gt;<strong> Select n° screen </strong>-&gt;<strong> set cursor to 0</strong>, then restart your MMI.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/splashscreenmmi3gp-6fcb5f6a.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>For <strong>MMI 3G</strong>: <strong>car</strong> -&gt; <strong>carcodingvehicle</strong> -&gt; <strong>configuration line</strong> -&gt; <em><strong>[standard] 2/5</strong> (Standard home screen)</em> then restart your MMI.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_6876-ad94c126.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>Your very own Splash Screen will appear!<br/>Many images are available in the zip file… both the original and modified ones.</p>\n<p><em>A problem?  </em>If the script doesn’t run the first time, try again. You’ve only copied the contents of the MMI_3G_3GP_SplashScreen folder? Do not copy the folder, just its contents!  <br/>For MMI 3G Basic: If your image does not appear or is truncated, resize the image to 400 by 240.</p>\n<hr/>\n<ul><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_A1-cca1d214.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_A1-quattro-d5c05d6b.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_A6-ec35ba13.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_A6-allroad-ecfb784b.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_A6-Hybrid-8b3bc272.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_A6L-da4efe88.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_A7-0413e2db.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_A8-b82aa2e7.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_A8-Hybrid-bf48c947.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_Q3-f5806bdd.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_Q5-137fb9fc.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_RS6-99c35be3.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_RS7-973708ca.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_RSQ3-82016453.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_RSQ5-4b2a2aa7.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_S1-8fca826d.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_S6-ff017200.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_S6-png_APR-b51955a9.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_S6-APR-5b67cc13.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_S7-1b8e075e.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_S8-1a7397d6.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_Vierge-e6bcc4e4.webp\"/></figure></li><li><figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMi-SplashScreens_AUDI_W12-9cbddbdf.webp\"/></figure></li></ul><a></a><a></a><a></a>","q7-4l-opening-closing-windows-with-remote-control":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Enables you to open and close the windows and sunroof using the remote control. </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong></strong> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click<strong>“46 – Comfort Module.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> –<em> </em>Select Channel <strong>61</strong>,<em> “Comfort Functions</em>,” from the drop-down list</p>\n<p><em>Add the following values:<br/><strong>+ 1</strong>: Close the windows using the remote control<br/><strong>+ 2</strong>: Open the windows using the remote control<br/><strong>+ 4</strong>: Close the sunroof using the remote control<br/><strong>+ 8</strong>: Open the sunroof using the remote control</em></p>","q7-4l-parking-aid-display-on-mmi":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to activate the radar display on the MMI with the Audi Parking System rear option only.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong></strong> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click<strong>“76 – Parking Assist.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “ <strong>Code 07.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – <em>Replace the second “0” (from the left) with a “2”.</em></p>\n<p><em>Ex: Replace “<strong>0001216</strong>” with “<strong>0201216</strong>”.</em></p>\n<p><em>Coding :</em><br/><em>0?xxxxx: Visual Display</em><br/><em>0 = without Visual Display on MMI</em><br/><em>2 = with Visual Display on MMI</em></p>","q7-4l-pilot-controlled-suspension-calibration":"<p class=\"empty\">No procedure text was published on the source page.</p>","q7-4l-rear-lights-activated-with-daytime-running-lights-drl":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Enables the rear lights to turn on when the daytime running lights (Scandinavian DRL) are activated. <br/><br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on <strong>“Coding – 07</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>5 –</strong> xxxxx? Country variant <br/><br/>1 – Rest of the World (RoW)<br/><strong>2 – Northern countries (Finland, Sweden, Norway, Denmark)</strong><br/>3 – USA (US)<br/>4 – Canada (CDN)</p>","q7-4l-reprogramming-a-new-battery":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to reprogram / recode the new battery of all its data after replacement.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Watch out! Depending on your calculator, select 61 or 19</strong> <strong>(CAN or UDS)</strong> <br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<h2>61-Batterie Regul. CAN </h2>\n<p>This procedure concerns the replacement of the battery in vehicles using a separate battery management control module.<br/>Address 61: Regul Battery. Labels: 4F0-910-181.lbl Reference SW: 4F0 910 181 E HW: 4F0 915 181 A Component: ENERGIEMANAGER H12 0490 Subsystem 1 – Part No: 000 915 105 C Component: von VA0 2502160103 Coding: 303030393135313035432056413032353032313630313033 Shop N °: WSC 54332 321 22222 </p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“61 – Battery Regul. </strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose the <strong>battery (slave) classified n°1</strong><br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – In<strong>“Coding battery</strong>” :  </p>\n<ul>\n<li>Enter the new Battery Part number (10 or 11 digits).</li>\n<li>Enter the new battery serial number (10 digits).</li>\n<li>Select the new battery supplier.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>[OK]<br/>[! Do – it]<br/>[Close Controller, Go Back – 06]</p>\n<p>Your new battery should now be coded, and the battery control module should be aware of the new battery.</p>\n<hr/>\n<h2>19-CAN Gateway using CAN</h2>\n<p>This procedure concerns battery replacement in vehicles using a battery management control module which is a slave / subsystem of the CAN gateway.Address 19: CAN Gateway (J533) Labels: 8T0-907-468.clb Reference SW: 8T0 907 468 Q HW: 8T0 907 468 L Component: GW-EBM 5CAN-M H10 0095 Subsystem 1 – Part No SW: 8K0 915 181 B HW: 8K0 915 181 B Component: J367-BDM H04 0150</p>\n<p>Installation of a new battery requires use of the [Long Adaptation-0A function] under the 19-CAN-Gateway control module. . Follow the on-screen instructions to enter the part number, supplier, serial number and any long new value.</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“19 – <strong>Gateway </strong>CAN</strong>”.<br/><br/> 4 – Click on<strong>“Long Adaptation-0A</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5 </strong>– Select <strong>Channel 04</strong></p>\n<p>VCED will populate instructions in the form of a pop-up balloon with formatting. For example:Format: nnnnnnnnnnn XXX zzzzzzzzzz N = battery part number (11 digits) X = battery supplier (3 digits) Z = battery serial number (10 digits) </p>\n<p>[Add to log] Saving the original value in a log is strongly recommended.<br/>Enter the New Battery details in the new field value.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Note, the new value must be 26 (alpha numeric) characters in total, including spaces! If in doubt, check the logbook for the original battery formatting details. </li>\n</ul>\n<p>[Test]<br/>[Save]<br/>The value has been accepted by the controller the new battery coding is complete<br/>[Done, Back]<br/>[Close Controller, Go Back – 06]</p>\n<hr/>\n<h2>19-CAN Gateway help (UDS / ODX)</h2>\n<p>This procedure concerns battery replacement in vehicles using a battery management control module which is a slave / subsystem of the CAN gateway.Address 19: CAN Gateway (J533) Labels: None Reference SW: 4G0 907 468 E HW: 4G0 907 468 A Component: J533 – Gateway H08 0213 ASAM Dataset: EV_GatewUDS 001025 Battery Monitoring Control Module: Subsystem 1 – Part No SW: 8×0 915 181 HW: 8×0 915 181 Component: J367-BDM H07 0140</p>\n<p>Installing a new battery requires the use of the [Adaptation-10 function] under the 19-CAN-Gateway control module. Use the drop-down menus to enter the part number, vendor, and serial number information located on the new battery. </p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“19 – CAN Gateway</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Adaptation batterie-Capacité nominal de la batterie</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu, but towards the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, choose a nominal value indicated on your battery, e.g.<strong>“70Ah</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“19 – CAN Gateway</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Adaptation batterie-Fabriquant de batterie</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, choose the corresponding brand:<br/>Ex: In the case of the VARTA E39, choose<strong>“VAO</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 3:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“19 – CAN Gateway</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Adaptation batterie-Numéro de série de la batterie</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu, but at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, enter the corresponding serial number:<br/>Warning, insert only the <strong>last 10 digits</strong> of the serial number.</p>\n<p>The value has been accepted by the controller the new battery coding is complete<br/>[Done, Back]<br/>[Close Controller, Go Back – 06]</p>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>Battery</strong></p>\n<p>The vehicle’s battery is housed in the engine compartment and protected by a battery tray. Battery size and design depend on engine version, equipment and national variant. Standard, EFB and AGM batteries are used.<br/>Vehicles with petrol engines and start/stop systems are fitted with EFB batteries, while vehicles with diesel engines and start/stop systems are fitted with AGM batteries.   Vehicles with stationary chauﬀage generally have an AGM battery.</p>\n<p><strong>EFB</strong></p>\n<p>An EFB (Enhanced Flooded Battery) is a reinforced wet battery. The positive plate inside the battery is coated with an additional polyester canvas. This gives the battery’s active mass additional support on the plate. The alternating cycle resistance of these batteries is superior to that of standard batteries. During charging, the EFB battery is treated like a standard battery.</p>\n<p><strong>AGM battery</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/batterie-agm-f4b81a74.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>In AGM batteries (short for Absorbent Glass Mat), the battery’s electrolyte is retained in a micro-porous glass mat. An AGM battery is not only even more resistant to alternating cycles than an EFB battery, but also watertight. When charging, follow the charger’s operating instructions and select the AGM battery program if necessary.</p>\n<p>In the case of AGM batteries, the automotive battery electrolyte is retained in a micro-porous glass mat. In addition to<br/>increased resistance to alternating cycles, an AGM battery is characterized by its good sealing properties. Waterproofing is of crucial importance<br/>, especially when the battery is installed in<br/>the passenger compartment. When charging, please follow the charger’s operating instructions and select the program for<br/>AGM battery, if applicable.</p>\n<p>Below we see the battery brand, serial number and manufacturer.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/batterie-124711ff.webp\"/></figure>"};
